  "circulation": "Yard is the orientation landmark. Two cell-block routes join front intake and rear cross passage. Mechanical manual releases on both sides of security gates prevent power failure or ghost action from making permanent traps. Upper galleries are narrow observational branches, not the only way out.",
  "systems": "Security gates, lighting and plant have explicit independent circuits. Metal galleries, concrete cell rows and open yard require distinct audio portals. Cell bays remain a later subdivision of each block, with stable child IDs.",
  "campaign": "Visitor records, medical accounts and guard rotas support contradictory history without equating incarceration with supernatural evil.",
  "refine": [
    "Lay out real individual cells and upper gallery voids; block volumes alone are not complete cell geometry.",
    "Test two-sided manual gate release during all power states before allowing hunts.",
    "Primary reference text inspected: https://www.nps.gov/places/000/alcatraz-cellhouse.htm \u2014 separate blocks and hospital; dimensions here are fictional game proposals."
  ],
